<title>USA: San Antonio feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</title>
<headline>San Antonio feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers were steady to $1.00 per cwt higher, except steers under 500 lbs, which were  $7.00-$9.00 higher, compared to Monday, USDA said. Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 300-600 lb feeder steers and heifers. Supply included around 10 percent cows and bulls, 12 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Receipts - 309    Last Week - 321   Last Year - 1,006</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-675 lbs 76.50-85.00; few 700-750 lbs 70.25-78.25; few 825-875 lbs 68.25-68.50. 70.25, pkg 75.50. Medium and Large 1-2 - 300-500 lbs 85.25-92.00, pkg 100.00; 550-675 lbs 88.50-78.25; few 725-800 lbs 64.00-68.50.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 500-600 lbs 75.00-86.00; 650-800 lbs 68.50- 74.25, pkg replacement quality 80.00. Medium and Large 1-2 - 500-600 lbs 65.25-70.50.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
